Imports:
  - Types:
      - NestContainer
      - InstanceWrapper
    From: packages/core/injector

Annotations: |
  Implements Nest's interceptor extension point: the runtime mechanism behind
  @UseInterceptors() and the NestInterceptor interface, used to wrap handler
  execution with cross-cutting behaviour (logging, caching, response mapping,
  timeout handling) on both the way in and the way out.

---

"InterceptorsConsumer()":
  location: interceptors-consumer.ts
  annotations: |
    Chains a resolved list of interceptors around the eventual route-handler call,
    each interceptor deciding whether and how to invoke the next one in the chain.
  methods:
    "intercept(interceptors: Array<any>, args: Array<any>, instance: any, callback: Object<string, any>, next: Object<string, any>, type: string) -> result: Promise<any>": |
      `interceptors`: NestInterceptor instances resolved for the current handler
      `args`: the handler's raw argument list, wrapped into an execution context
      `instance`: the controller instance handling the request
      `callback`: the handler method being intercepted
      `next`: a function that ultimately invokes the route handler itself

      Algorithm:
      1. An empty `interceptors` list calls `next` immediately
      2. Build one execution context shared by every interceptor in the chain
      3. Compose a right-to-left chain where each interceptor's call handler invokes
         the next interceptor in line (and the last one's call handler invokes `next`)
      4. Invoke the first interceptor with that composed chain and return its
         resulting stream
    "createContext(args: Array<any>, instance: any, callback: Object<string, any>) -> context: Object<string, any>": |
      Build the execution context shared by every interceptor invoked for this
      request.

"InterceptorsContextCreator(container: NestContainer, config: any)":
  location: interceptors-context-creator.ts
  annotations: |
    Resolves the ordered list of NestInterceptor instances that apply to one
    handler: method-level interceptors, controller-level interceptors, and global
    interceptors from `config`, combined in that precedence order.

    `container`: `NestContainer` from Imports, used to look up an already
    instantiated interceptor by its class and owning module
    `config`: supplies global interceptors registered on the application
  methods:
    "create(instance: any, callback: Object<string, any>, module: string, contextId: Object<string, any>, inquirerId: string) -> interceptors: Array<any>": |
      Collect the interceptor metadata attached to `callback` and its class, resolve
      each entry to a live interceptor instance via getInterceptorInstance, and
      drop entries that are not valid NestInterceptor implementations.
    "getInterceptorInstance(metatype: Object<string, any>, contextId: Object<string, any>, inquirerId: string) -> interceptor: any": |
      An interceptor passed as a plain object with an intercept method is used
      as-is; an interceptor passed as a class is looked up in the current module's
      injectables by `metatype` and resolved through its `InstanceWrapper` from
      Imports for the given `contextId`.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Documents the interceptor extension mechanism: resolving NestInterceptor
  instances for a handler (`InterceptorsContextCreator`) and chaining them around
  the handler call (`InterceptorsConsumer`). core/router composes this cell with
  core/guards and core/pipes to build the full per-request execution pipeline.
